#! ia 1.0

@capability hook-method
  meaning
    says "Work with hook records under the IA methodology: the hook-method playbook's orient, plan, act and learn cells for finding, planning, changing and checking a hook. It grants no authority; the workspace's mandates decide what the participant may change."
    answers "Which procedure does an agent follow for a hook?"
  composition
    playbooks [@playbook hook-method]
  execution
    effects [read, local-write]

@playbook hook-method
  meaning
    says "How an agent works with hook records, each a host event, tool or path selection and guard message, whose registration and guard need a host adapter: orient through ia position --word hook and the word's schema, plan through the owner of the word, change records only through ia preview, ia author and ia validate, and leave the account reconciled."
    answers "How does an agent work with hook records?"
  subject
    subject-word hook
  cognition
    orient
      primary Attention
      Attention means "Run ia position --word hook at the seat the work concerns, read the hook records it points at with ia read, and run ia vocabulary hook --schema for the sections and fields a hook carries."
      Inference means "Read the hook's event, selection and guard message."
      Decision means "hook is a word of hook-authoring-system: when the seat is not that system or a workspace that composes it, re-seat with ia position --seat floor/definition/system/hook-authoring-system before going on; its steward pointer is to read, not to invoke."
      Learning means "Read the observations and improvements earlier work left on these hook records before repeating it."
    plan
      primary Inference
      Attention means "Restate what the hook must satisfy: the intent, the blocking rules and the mandate at the seat, and the ceiling of any provisional foundation."
      Inference means "Choose the event and the narrowest tool or path selection, and write a guard message that says what to do instead."
      Decision means "Extend an existing hook through its owner where one covers the need, and bring each consequential choice to the person with a recommendation."
      Learning means "Say how the hook will be judged and what would leave it inconclusive."
    act
      primary Decision
      Attention means "Read what ia preview compiles for the hook; a refusal means the plan is wrong about the record, not that the check is in the way."
      Inference means "Author the hook's event, selection and message; registering it with the host is the host adapter's job."
      Decision means "Change hook records only through ia preview hook <name> <field>=<value>..., then ia author with the same form and the digest preview returned, then ia validate; use --set or --relate the same way for one field or relationship."
      Learning means "Keep each refusal with its code, fix it within the step, and preview again."
    learn
      primary Learning
      Attention means "Run ia validate and the checks that apply, report them verbatim, and say which claims they evidence and which stay unevaluated."
      Inference means "Once the host registers it, check that the hook fires only where intended; a declared hook is not a registered one."
      Decision means "Reconcile the records that cite or depend on the hook, and leave the handoff packet method-handoff-packet describes."
      Learning means "Propose what the work taught to the owners concerned, as method-improvement-lifecycle describes, or state that there is none."
